Taking an armed Irq's notification leaves it armed,
so its line would fire into a notification that is gone,
and a destroy of its pool would leave the count of armed sources counting it;
an Irq without a notification is disarmed.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: irq without a notification is armed

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -365,7 +365,6 @@ void irq_signal(struct irq *irq)
 void irq_drop(struct cap *signalled)
 {
     struct irq *irq = signalled_irq(signalled);
-    irq_set_bits(irq, 0);
     /* Only the controller's lines have a mask. */
     if (line_on_controller(irq->line)) {
         irq_enable(irq->line, false);
